1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:00,500
Hi.

2
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:04,100
It's time to talk about feedback.

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:12,440
How to give a constructive feedback at work and how to use modal verbs for feedback.

4
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:14,910
Let's go.

5
00:00:14,910 --> 00:00:17,280
So what is feedback?

6
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:26,550
Feedback is helpful information or criticism that is given to someone to say what can be done to improve

7
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:29,790
a performance, product or process.

8
00:00:30,240 --> 00:00:33,450
Key word here is to improve.

9
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:34,830
All right.

10
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:43,710
So at work, you can give feedback to your coworker, your manager, your HR, or to a junior employee

11
00:00:43,710 --> 00:00:46,170
about work or performance.

12
00:00:46,170 --> 00:00:55,200
And you can give feedback about a project, about performance code, about someone's behavior or about

13
00:00:55,200 --> 00:00:57,720
the general process in a company.

14
00:00:58,380 --> 00:01:02,310
So tip number one for giving a good feedback.

15
00:01:02,340 --> 00:01:10,710
Give feedback privately in person, face to face, especially if it's a negative feedback or criticism.

16
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:13,290
All right.

17
00:01:13,290 --> 00:01:17,970
Tip number two, prepare the person for the feedback.

18
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:22,980
Use phrases like, Hi, do you have a minute to talk?

19
00:01:23,340 --> 00:01:25,230
Can we discuss something?

20
00:01:25,440 --> 00:01:27,600
Could I have a word with you?

21
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:32,220
Pause the video and repeat these sentences.

22
00:01:33,030 --> 00:01:34,410
Nicely done.

23
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,090
Next tip.

24
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:40,350
Start your feedback by saying thanks to the person.

25
00:01:40,590 --> 00:01:44,580
Use phrases like Thank you for meeting with me.

26
00:01:44,880 --> 00:01:48,090
Thank you for taking the time to meet with me.

27
00:01:48,330 --> 00:01:52,320
I am glad we could meet to discuss something.

28
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:56,070
Pause the video and repeat the phrases.

29
00:01:57,930 --> 00:01:58,670
Okay.

30
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:05,190
When giving feedback, talk about a specific event or issue problem.

31
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:11,790
It's a bad example to say something like You always interrupt people.

32
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:15,810
Try to avoid words like always all the time.

33
00:02:15,930 --> 00:02:24,270
Instead, you can say yesterday when we had a meeting, you were interrupting me a couple of times.

34
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:29,940
So here you say the specific date and specific event.

35
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:35,140
Use modal verbs for your feedback.

36
00:02:35,170 --> 00:02:42,850
Modal words like shoot would or could but avoid using word must.

37
00:02:42,880 --> 00:02:46,300
It sounds rude and not professional.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:56,790
For instance, instead of saying the design is awful, you can say something like the design is fine,

39
00:02:56,790 --> 00:03:01,140
but I would change would is a modal verb.

40
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:03,750
I don't like the project.

41
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:05,790
Bad way of giving feedback.

42
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:14,040
Instead, you can say I would be more satisfied on a project with more challenging technologies.

43
00:03:14,070 --> 00:03:15,240
Again, we used.

44
00:03:15,280 --> 00:03:19,950
Would your level of jazz is very low.

45
00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:20,880
Wrong?

46
00:03:20,910 --> 00:03:27,270
Instead, say I think you should work on your jazz skill improvement.

47
00:03:27,300 --> 00:03:30,330
Here we used modal verb should.

48
00:03:31,710 --> 00:03:32,670
All right.

49
00:03:32,790 --> 00:03:40,890
When giving feedback, tell what impact result this event or behavior had.

50
00:03:41,070 --> 00:03:49,080
For example, you say yesterday when we had a meeting, you were interrupting me a couple of times.

51
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,340
So you give feedback.

52
00:03:50,370 --> 00:03:52,500
You tell about specific event.

53
00:03:52,590 --> 00:03:56,040
And here is the result.

54
00:03:56,190 --> 00:04:01,500
And I felt frustrated and it was difficult for me to focus.

55
00:04:02,610 --> 00:04:03,450
Okay.

56
00:04:05,250 --> 00:04:10,710
When giving feedback, suggest improvements or help.

57
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:17,130
You can finish your feedback by saying Let me know if you need more advice or help.

58
00:04:17,400 --> 00:04:20,640
I hope this feedback was useful for you.

59
00:04:20,850 --> 00:04:25,170
If you have questions, feel free to get in touch.

60
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:29,340
Pause the video and repeat these sentences.

61
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:33,130
Nicely done.

62
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:36,250
Okay, but how to receive feedback.

63
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:39,670
Always thank for the feedback.

64
00:04:39,700 --> 00:04:42,150
Say thank you for your feedback.

65
00:04:42,160 --> 00:04:43,880
I appreciate it.

66
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,700
I will work on that.

67
00:04:45,730 --> 00:04:48,640
Thanks for bringing this up.

68
00:04:48,970 --> 00:04:52,360
Pause the video and repeat the phrases.

69
00:04:54,290 --> 00:04:55,010
Good.

70
00:04:55,190 --> 00:04:58,210
Also, let's learn how to give advice.

71
00:04:58,220 --> 00:05:05,030
So this is my friend Mike and he received a negative feedback about his PHP level.

72
00:05:05,330 --> 00:05:09,560
I want to help him and I want to give him some advice.

73
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:11,960
Okay.

74
00:05:12,050 --> 00:05:16,730
I will use phrases like I think you should.

75
00:05:16,730 --> 00:05:19,730
And if I were you, I would.

76
00:05:19,760 --> 00:05:24,890
So Mike, I think you should take a PHP course.

77
00:05:24,920 --> 00:05:27,920
I think you should find a mentor.

78
00:05:28,070 --> 00:05:32,180
I think you should write a pet project on PHP.

79
00:05:32,960 --> 00:05:38,420
Or I can say if I were you I would read a book on PHP.

80
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:43,190
If I were you, I would learn from senior developers.

81
00:05:43,430 --> 00:05:46,880
Pause the video and repeat the phrases.

82
00:05:48,630 --> 00:05:49,630
Nicely done.

83
00:05:49,650 --> 00:05:50,680
Thank you.

84
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:55,530
Find more exercises and examples of feedback in your file.

85
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,490
See you.

86
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:57,030
Bye.
